records.qn_text:
(a) the number of private space startups registered and authorized in the country by IN-SPACe, so far;
(b) whether Government has formulated any equal opportunity policy for private companies to utilize the infrastructure and launch pads at ISRO's Satish Dhawan Space Centre, Sriharikota; and
(c) the number of commercial rockets proposed to be launched by Indian private companies during the next two years?

(a) whether the newly established Centre of Excellence in Coimbatore is conducting any specific scientific study to mitigate conflict in the Lemru Elephant Reserve and other corridors in Chhattisgarh;
(b) whether the Central Government is formulating any action plan for developing new safe elephant corridors and preventing railway accidents in the State using the data of the study; and
(c) the quantum of central financial assistance provided to the Chhattisgarh Forest Department during the current financial year for procurement of drones, thermal sensors and AI-based monitoring technologies?

(a) the present progress status of the 'e-Sakshya' mobile application developed by the Ministry for the mandatory videography and photography of crime scenes following the implementation of three new criminal laws in the country;
(b) whether Government has provided the necessary smartphones, internet connectivity and cloud storage facilities to all remote police stations and investigating officers across the country to operate this application; and
(c) the security protocols adopted to ensure the security, prevention of tampering and legal admissibility of digital evidence?

(a) the primary objective of the 'Seafarer-First' initiative recently launched by Government and the specific maritime regions covered therein;
(b) whether Government has developed any real-time tracking system to keep moment-to-moment information about Indian sailors passing through crisis-hit areas; and
(c) whether this tracking system would apply equally to Indian nationals deployed on foreign-flagged vessels?

(a) whether it is a fact that land was acquired for NTPC Limited's Lara project and made available on lease subject to compliance with Chhattisgarh's Model Rehabilitation Policy;
(b) whether it is also a fact that a clear provision or mention has been made in the agreement for providing employment to eligible persons affected by land acquisition, if so, the details thereof; and 
(c) if so, the total number of regular posts filled till now and the number of members of families affected by the land acquisition who have been granted regular appointments?

(a) the total number of trains targeted to be operated under the 'Hydrogen for Heritage' scheme in the country;  
(b) whether Government has identified those historic and hill routes where traditional diesel engines will be replaced and these green trains will be operated;  
(c) the names of these routes and the timeline by which this entire scheme will be implemented in a phased manner; and  
(d) the estimated annual percentage reduction in diesel imports and carbon emissions of the railways by operating these trains?

(a) whether the recently launched 'National Human-Wildlife Conflict portal' is active in elephant-affected districts of Chhattisgarh such as Sarguja, Raigarh and Mahasamund;
(b) the technical arrangements made through the portal to track the real-time location of elephant herds in Chhattisgarh and send advance warnings to local villagers; and
(c) the details of loss of life, property and crops due to human-elephant conflict in Chhattisgarh during the last three years, year-wise?

(a) the current plan for deploying forensic mobile vans in all districts across the country for the collection of evidence in offences punishable with imprisonment of seven years or more under the new laws;
(b) the total number of forensic mobile vans allocated so far to various States across the country and the types of advanced digital and scientific equipment provided in these vans; and
(c) whether Government is providing any special national financial assistance for the recruitment of independent forensic experts and technical manpower, in addition to the police departments for the operation of these vans?

(a) whether Government is aware that one in three bacterial infections in the country, has become resistant to common antibiotics;
(b) whether Government has issued any stringent guidelines to States under the recently released ‘National Action Plan on AMR 2.0’ to prevent the illegal sale of antibiotics without a prescription; and
(c) whether Government has proposed mandatory blue strip labelling on all antimicrobial medicines under the draft notification issued in January, 2026, to facilitate their easy identification at pharmacy counters and prevent its misuse?

(a) the current status of the construction of the permanent campus of the newly established National Institute of Fashion Technology (NIFT) in Nava Raipur;
(b) the amount of funds released by Government so far for this institute; and
(c) whether there is any plan to start a special research center or course in this campus for the skill development of the local tribals of Chhattisgarh and traditional Kosa silk weavers?

(a) whether Government is aware of the fact that tomatoes and other horticultural crops get spoiled on a large scale due to the lack of cold storage and cold chain network in Chhattisgarh;
(b) if so, the plans of Government to prevent it; and
(c) the current status of the approved Mega Food Parks and Agro-Processing Clusters in Chhattisgarh and the timeline by which these are expected to become fully operational?

(a) whether the naxal-affected Bastar and Sarguja regions have failed to develop as tourism destinations due to lack of basic amenities, despite possessing immense natural and cultural potential and if so, the details thereof;
(b) whether Government proposes to provide a separate special package for improving connectivity, road construction and other development works under the 'Swadesh Darshan' scheme for tourist sites in the regions; and
(c) if not, the amount allocated for connectivity, road construction and other works under the 'Swadesh Darshan' scheme for tourist sites in the regions,scheme-wise?

(a) whether it is a fact that the cost of treatment for several rare diseases, including Spinal Muscular Atrophy, Amyotrophic Lateral Sclerosis/Motor Neuron Disease and Myasthenia Gravis in the country runs into crores of rupees per annum, which is completely beyond the reach of the common citizens;
(b) the present status of the one-time financial assistance of ?50 lakh provided to eligible patients under the 'National Policy for Rare Diseases' (NPRD) and the number of patients benefited thereunder during the last two years; and
(c) whether Government is considering complete exemption from customs duty and GST levied on life-saving drugs?

(a) whether Government has prepared a mandatory national roadmap for blending two per cent Sustainable Aviation Fuel (SAF) by 2028 and five per cent by 2030, in alignment with the International Civil Aviation Organization's 'Carbon Offsetting and Reduction Scheme for International Aviation' (CORSIA);
(b) if so, the annual volume of bio-jet fuel that the country's oil marketing companies would need to produce to achieve the five per cent blending target by 2030; and
(c) whether Government proposes to provide any tax exemptions or subsidies to shield domestic airlines from the financial burden associated with the use of this expensive fuel?

(a) number of Self Help Groups (SHGs) formed in the country till date under Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana- National Rural Livelihood Mission (NRLM) and number of rural women associated with them;
(b) the details of the special loan facilities being provided to women in Self Help Groups for financial literacy, technical skills, and starting micro-enterprises with the goal of making them Lakhpati Didi; and
(c) total turnover recorded during last one year through 'Saras Aajeevika Stores' and e-commerce platforms from the marketing of the products manufactured by these women's groups?

(a) the total number of villages adopted so far under the Saansad Adarsh ??Gram Yojana (SAGY) by the present Hon'ble Members of the Lok Sabha and Rajya Sabha, the details thereof, State-wise;
(b) whether it is a fact that in the absence of a separate and independent budgetary allocation for the Scheme, difficulties are being faced in undertaking development works in the adopted villages through convergence with other Government schemes; and
(c) whether Government is considering any amendments to the guidelines of the Scheme with a view to make it more effective and outcome-oriented?

(a) the current status of women labour force participation rate in the country according to the latest data from the Periodic Labour Force Survey (PLFS), and the specific efforts being made to increase it;  
(b) the number of children rescued from various industries across the country (especially the firecracker industry, brick kilns, and hotels/dhabas) and rehabilitated under the National Child Labour Project for the complete eradication of child labour during the last two years; and  
(c) the State-wise details of legal action taken and imprisonment/fines imposed against employers dragging children for labour?

(a) the current status of implementation of new Labour Codes;
(b) the number of States/Union Territories which have, so far, drafted and notified their respective State Rules under the Codes; and
(c) whether Government is holding any tripartite talks to address the objections raised by certain State Governments or central trade unions regarding specific provisions of the Codes?

(a) the total number of tribal citizens screened so far under the National Sickle Cell Anemia Elimination Mission for the elimination of sickle cell anemia disease widely prevalent among the tribal population;

(b) the  details of the persons found to be suffering from Sickle Cell Disease (SCD) or carrying sickle cell trait during the screening, State-wise and age-wise and the special medical assistance being provided to them; and

(c) the steps taken by Government to provide genetic counselling to newly-married couples and pregnant women in the affected areas?

(a) number of electric buses allocated so far under the PM-eBus Sewa Scheme to make public transport pollution-free in various cities of the country, State-wise details thereof;  
(b) whether State Road Transport Corporations (SRTCs) are facing difficulties in operating and maintaining these electric buses due to financial crises; and  
(c) number of vehicles that have been scrapped so far under the Voluntary Vehicle Scrapping Policy implemented by Government to remove old and polluting vehicles in the country?

(a)  institution-wise details of approved posts and current vacancies of faculty in the country's Central Universities, Indian Institutes of Technology (IITs), and National Institutes of Technology (NITs); 
(b) number of appointments made so far under the special recruitment campaigns run to fill backlog positions for reserved categories (SC, ST, OBC, EWS) in these premier institutions ; and
(c) the alternative arrangements made by Government to prevent the adverse impact on the quality of higher education and research work due to the shortage of faculty members?

(a) whether any special policy has been formulated to increase the distribution of 'Shree Anna' (coarse cereals such as Pearl Millet, Finger Millet and Sorghum) through Fair Price Shops (FPS) for promoting nutritious grains;
(b) the States which have procured coarse cereals for the Central Pool during the current year and the budgetary provisions made to ensure the Minimum Support Price (MSP) for farmers; and
(c) whether Government is considering to provide an option to ration card holders in urban areas to choose millets/coarse cereals in place of wheat and rice as per their preference?

(a) the total number of State-wise alerts (triggers) generated by the Mining Surveillance System (MSS) regarding suspected illegal mining activity during the last two years;
(b) out of the alerts received, the number of cases in which physical verification has been carried out and action taken by the State Governments at the ground level; and
(c) the steps being taken to curb illegal mining, transportation and storage in the country and to make the States more accountable under Section 23C of the Mines and Minerals (Development and Regulation) Act (MMDR Act)?

(a) the number of objections received from stakeholders during the public consultation period in respect of draft Central Rules relating to the new Labour Codes;
(b) whether Government has prepared a subject-wise compilation of the comments received and placed the same in the public domain;
(c) whether any changes have been made in the final rules based on these representations and if so, the details thereof; and
(d) the State/Union Territory-wise status of framing and notification of respective State Rules under each Code and the steps taken by Government to ensure harmonization and timely implementation thereof?

(a) whether Government has conducted any study in recent times on the rate of deforestation in the country especially in  Chhattisgarh and if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor;
(b) whether Government has conducted any study to monitor the effect of climate change on traditional forest dwellers and if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor; and
(c) the details of measures taken by Government to balance economic growth with the climate goals, especially given its dependence on coal and the needs of its growing population?

(a) the year-wise and State-wise total number of deaths reported during sewer and septic tank cleaning operations during the last five years;
(b) the number of such cases in which compensation has been paid as per Supreme Court directions, the amount disbursed in each case and the number of cases where compensation remains pending;
(c) whether any assessment has been conducted to identify the causes of continued sewer deaths despite statutory prohibition of hazardous manual cleaning and the findings thereof; and
(d) the number of mechanised sewer cleaning machines procured and deployed during last five years and whether any time bound plan exists to eliminate manual entry into sewers?

(a) the year-wise and State-wise length of National Highways constructed during last five years, along with total construction expenditure and the amount spent on their maintenance and repair within five years of completion;
(b) the year-wise number of accidents and fatalities on National Highways since 2021 where potholes, surface defects or incomplete construction were recorded as contributing factors; and
(c) whether any contractor has been penalised or blacklisted due to premature road deterioration or poor-quality construction and the details thereof?

(a) the number of complaints received regarding financial irregularities, incomplete works or non functional tap connections under Jal Jeevan Mission since 2023, State-wise and year-wise;
(b) the number of habitations reported receiving supply below prescribed service level norms since 2023;
(c) the number of districts in water stressed, desert, hilly or tribal areas where source sustainability issues have been recorded as on date, year-wise; and
(d) whether the Mission timeline has been extended in any State due to slow progress or technical capacity constraints and the details thereof?

(a) the year-wise number of vacancies reported by scheduled airlines and whether any assessment of shortage has been conducted since 2023;
(b) the year-wise number of aircraft grounded due to technical defects or maintenance delays since 2023;
(c) the year-wise number of safety violation notices issued by the Directorate General of Civil Aviation (DGCA) relating to Flight Duty Time Limitation (FDTL) norms in since 2023; and
(d) the State-wise number of airports operating above declared capacity and the number of operational airports with passenger utilisation below 25 per cent of capacity?

(a) the revenue earned from advertisements displayed inside trains, on train exteriors and at railway stations since 2022, zone-wise and year-wise;
(b) the list of advertising agencies or vendors empanelled or awarded contracts for such advertisements during this period, zone-wise;
(c) the details of advertisements displayed and the duration of such display since 2022, brand-wise;
(d) whether any guidelines exist regarding content standards and approval mechanisms for advertisements displayed in trains, if so, the details thereof; and
(e) the number of complaints received regarding objectionable advertisements since 2022, year-wise?

(a) the total number of rail level crossings as on date, indicating the number that are manned, interlocked, Road Over Bridges or Road Under Bridges;
(b) the number of level crossings eliminated since 2021, along with details of mode of elimination;
(c) the number of accidents and fatalities at level crossings since 2021, State/UT-wise and year-wise; and
(d) the total funds allocated and utilised for level crossing elimination and safety works during the period?

(a) the total land required and land acquired for projects under Bharatmala Pariyojana during last five years, State-wise and project-wise, as on date;
(b) State-wise and year-wise total compensation assessed and disbursed for such land acquisition;
(c) the number of cases where compensation or rehabilitation and resettlement payments remain pending beyond statutory timelines under the Right to Fair Compensation and Transparency in Land Acquisition, Rehabilitation and Resettlement Act, 2013; and
(d) whether any review has been conducted on cost escalation in Bharatmala projects due to delays in land acquisition and the project-wise extent of such escalation?

(a) the number of districts that failed to conduct the mandatory four District Development Coordination and Monitoring Committee (DISHA) meetings per year during each of the last three financial years;
(b) the number of districts which did not hold even a single DISHA meeting in 2024–25 and 2025–26;
(c) the reasons furnished by District Collectors for such failure, State-wise; and
(d) whether fund released under Centrally Sponsored Schemes (CSS) were withheld or deferred in such districts as envisaged under DISHA monitoring provisions?

(a) whether Government has undertaken two revision of passenger fares during the financial year 2025–26, if so, the dates, categories of trains, and classes of travel to which each revision applied;
(b) the State-wise details of stations and services affected by these fare revisions;
(c) whether Government assessed the cumulative financial impact of multiple fare increases on passengers, particularly low- and middle-income commuters, prior to implementing the second revision; and
(d) manner in which Government plans to revise the system without hindering service to passengers who cannot afford to pay the twice-increased amount?

(a) the job-role-wise demand data used to approve training targets under Pradhan Mantri Kaushal Vikas Yojana (PMKVY) during each of the last three phases;
(b) the number of districts that submitted District Skill Development Plans (DSDPs) prior to allocation of PMKVY targets, year-wise;
(c) the percentage of PMKVY targets that were allocated without reference to DSDPs; and
(d) the State-wise delays in release and utilisation of PMKVY funds under the State component?

(a) the year-wise data since Sagarmala’s launch on projects added, projects dropped or put on hold and projects re-scoped due to delays or infeasibility;
(b) the project-wise list of the 131 projects which are in development stage, including original approval date, latest revised completion date and present stage of execution;
(c) the details of original project cost and the latest estimated cost for the 131 projects still at the development stage; and
(d) how many projects have been delayed by more than three years solely due to land acquisition issues and the cumulative cost escalation attributable to these delays?

(a) the year-wise growth rate of Private Final Consumption Expenditure (PFCE) for rural and urban areas separately during Financial Year 2022-23 to 2025-26;
(b) the share of rural and urban consumption in total PFCE for the same period;
(c) the year-wise growth rate of consumption loans disaggregated by rural and urban borrowers for the last three years; and
(d) the total outstanding value of consumption credit in rural and urban areas as on 31st December 2025?

(a) whether Government is aware of the disproportionate surge in unsecured loans compared to industrial credit;
(b) if so, the year-wise details since 2021 of the total volume of unsecured personal loans disbursed by Scheduled Commercial Banks and NBFCs in the country;
(c) the current share of unsecured credit in the overall retail lending portfolio; and
(d) what regulatory measures Government is taking to mitigate systemic risks arising from this growth?

BPN

(a) the total number of textile and apparel manufacturing units that have been opened, closed and remained operational in the last five years, year-wise and State/UT-wise;
(b) employment generated by the textile sector during this period, including gender-wise distribution; 
(c) whether Government has identified any key barriers to global competitiveness; and 
(d) if so, measures Government is taking to support MSME units in the textile sector?

(a) the total number of complaints received from farmers regarding non-payment or delayed payment of claims under the Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana (PMFBY) in the last five years, year-wise, State/UT-wise;
(b) whether Government has taken any steps to improve the accuracy and transparency of crop damage assessment under PMFBY, if so, the details thereof;
(c) whether Government is considering amendments to the scheme to address payment inconsistencies, improve accountability of insurance companies; and
(d) if so, the details of measures taken to restore farmer confidence in the crop insurance scheme?

(a) whether Government is aware of inadequate sports infrastructure and limited training facilities available across the country including Chhattisgarh;
(b) whether any proposals have been received from various State/UT Administrations for the development or upgradation of sports infrastructure, including construction of indoor stadiums, outdoor grounds, swimming facilities and youth training centres;
(c) if so, the State/UT-wise details thereof and the current status of such proposals;
(d) the number of Government-funded training centres, academies and coaches available across India, sports-wise; and
(e) the State/UT-wise number of athletes who have received support at such centres during the last five years?

(a) the forest area (in hectares) diverted for the mining projects, including details of primary rainforest and biodiversity-rich zones cleared or proposed to be cleared;
(b) whether Government has conducted a cumulative environmental impact assessment of the project, considering its potential effects on indigenous communities, marine ecosystems and endemic species; and
(c) whether the compensatory afforestation proposed under the Forest (Conservation) Act has been completed and if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the number of postfacto or retrospective environmental clearances granted since 2021, year-wise and State/UT-wise;
(b) the details of penalties collected from such cases, if any;
(c) the year-wise and State/UT-wise details of projects granted clearance despite being flagged by the Ministry’s own Expert Appraisal Committees;
(d) whether Government has conducted any assessment of ecological and economic consequences of regularising such projects; and
(e) if so, the findings thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the outstanding balances for all ongoing North-East Special Infrastructure Development Scheme (NESIDS) projects as on 31 December 2025, State-wise and sector-wise;
(b) the identified  projects where more than 50 per cent of approved cost remains unspent despite receiving sanctions more than two years ago;
(c) the number of projects that are currently delayed beyond the original completion timeline, State-wise; and
(d) the details of sectoral allocation since its inception, year-wise?

(a) whether Government has taken cognizance of serious governance lapses in the National Skill Development Corporation (NSDC);
(b) if so, details of complaints filed against officials for alleged embezzlement of public funds during the last five years, year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise;
(c) total number of FIRs registered against training partners under PMKVY during the last five years, the value of misappropriated funds and the number of entities blacklisted, year-wise and State-wise/UT-wise; and
(d) whether Government has initiated any inquiry to address systemic irregularities in the Skill India Mission, if so, the details thereof and if not, the reasons therefor?

(a) the State-wise/UT-wise number of Panchayats that have adopted the SabhaSaar initiative;
(b) the State-wise/UT-wise number of Panchayats functionaries trained in using the SabhaSaar platform;
(c) whether the AI model powering SabhaSaar transmits or stores data on external servers or via third-party service providers, along with the names of such providers;
(d) whether the Ministry has issued any data protection and privacy guidelines for SabhaSaar, particularly concerning consent and secure storage of audio-visual records; and
(e) what measurable indicators have been created on the portal to track Gram Sabha frequency, attendance and action taken using SabhaSaar data?

(a) the State-wise shortfall between Budget Estimates, Revised Estimates and Actual Expenditure under Pradhan Mantri Matsya Sampada Yojana (PMMSY) during the last three financial years;
(b) the number of States that failed to comply with SNA-SPARSH guidelines, year-wise and the specific nature of non-compliance;
(c) the State-wise allocation versus actual expenditure under the Scheduled Castes Sub-Plan (SCSP) component of PMMSY from 2022-23 to 2024-25; and
(d) the number of States that failed to submit proposals under SCSP during this period?

(a) the number of Government schools with functional computer labs and internet connectivity, along with the total number of Government school, State-wise/UT-wise;
(b) Government schools offering AI or digital literacy in their curriculum;
(c) whether national guidelines or pedagogical standards exist for AI education at the school level, if so, details thereof and if not, reasons therefor;
(d) the  number of Government school teachers trained in AI-related instruction and whether such training includes subject-specific capacity building, State-wise/UT-wise;
(e) whether learning outcome assessments have been conducted to evaluate these programmes; and
(f) the steps taken to prevent widening of digital divides due to disparities in infrastructure and teacher training?

(a) the number of education loan applications received, sanctioned, rejected and withdrawn, bank-wise and State-wise, during the last three financial years;
(b) whether Government has analysed the reasons for the significant gap between loan sanctions and actual disbursements under PM-Vidyalaxmi, if so, details thereof;
(c) the number of complaints received regarding illegal collateral or third-party guarantee demands for loans below the collateral-free threshold, State-wise;
(d) the number of higher-education institutions formally empanelled or linked with banks for education loan facilitation; and
(e) whether institutions in Tier-II and Tier-III cities show lower facilitation rates, if so, details thereof?

(a) whether Government has taken note of the December, 2025 report of Parliamentary Committee on energy which pointed out that while India has 243 GW of installed renewable energy capacity, the country currently has only about 5.5 GW of energy storage capacity, against a projected requirement of 61 GW by 2030;
(b) if so, what specific steps are being taken to bridge this gap, including support for domestic research and manufacturing of storage technologies; and
(c) the reasons for Power Purchase Agreements remaining unsigned for nearly 44 GW of solar capacity as of June 2025, despite bids having been invited?

(a) the total value of loans written off by Public Sector Banks (PSBs) from Financial Year 2021-22 to Financial Year 2025-26, with PSB- wise and year-wise breakup for the last five years;
(b) the details of top 50 largest corporate accounts written off by PSBs during this period, bank-wise; and
(c) the value of loans written off and waived specifically for farmers in the same period, PSB-wise and year-wise?

(a) whether Government has taken note of reports regarding illegal massage centres and spas operating under the guise of Ayurvedic or Ayush clinics, including instances involving immoral trafficking;
(b) whether any licensing, inspection or monitoring mechanism exists to verify the authenticity of such establishments using Ayush nomenclature, if so, the number of registrations cancelled or suspended in the last three years;
(c) whether the Ministry coordinates with State Governments and law-enforcement agencies to prevent misuse of Ayush systems for illegal activities; and
(d) the steps taken or proposed to strengthen regulation, ensure practitioner accountability and protect the credibility of Ayush systems?

(a) the State-wise number of agricultural feeders that were originally assessed, sanctioned and actually separated under Deen Dayal Upadhyaya Gram Jyoti Yojana (DDUGJY);
(b) whether Government has assessed the impact of incomplete feeder separation on hours of supply to non-agricultural rural consumers;
(c) the State-wise number of projects where award of work exceeded prescribed timelines by 12 months and 24 months; and
(d) the number of instances where funds were released prior to fulfilment of mandatory pre-conditions such as agreements and State contribution?

(a) the basis on which the estimated number of un-electrified households was revised downward during SAUBHAGYA implementation;
(b) State-wise number of households currently identified as de-electrified or non-functional connections;
(c) the amount of extra-budgetary borrowings raised by Rural Electrification Corporation (REC) under SAUBHAGYA and related schemes; and
(d) the interest burden incurred on unutilised funds?

(a) whether Government has prepared district-wise remedial action plans for groundwater contamination in districts identified as hotspots in the CGWB Annual Ground Water Quality Report, 2024;
(b) the number of Jal Jeevan Mission habitations located in districts where groundwater contamination exceeds permissible limits; 
(c) the percentage of such habitations receiving treated or alternative safe water sources; and
(d) whether districts with over 40 per cent nitrate exceedance have been mapped against fertiliser consumption and cropping intensity data, if so, the corrective advisories or restrictions that have been introduced?

(a) whether there is a huge potential available for wildlife and forest tourism in the country particularly in Bastar region of Chhattisgarh;
(b) if so, the steps taken to tap the tourism potential across various States of the country including the Bastar region of the State; and 
(c) the measures proposed/implemented to promote Bastar region as a major destination for ecotourism to explore wildlife and forest tourism?

(a) whether Government has undertaken any assessment of ecological degradation, deforestation and biodiversity loss in the Bastar region of Chhattisgarh during the last three years and the current year;
(b) the details of funds allocated and disbursed under centrally sponsored schemes such as the National Afforestation Programme, Green India Mission and Compensatory Afforestation Fund Management and Planning Authority (CAMPA) for projects in the State, particularly in Bastar region; and
(c) the details of steps being taken by Government to strengthen central monitoring, enforcing compliance with environmental safeguards and ensuring time-bound restoration of forest and catchment areas in the Bastar region?

(a) the details of staff employed in Group A, B and C posts and the vacancies in different categories in Ministry;
(b) the details of backlog vacancies in SC, ST and OBC categories;
(c) the details of the action plan to fill up backlog and regular vacancies to run schemes smoothly; and
(d) the details of the number of employees retired and the number of newly recruited employees during the last three years?

(a) whether the Ministry has reviewed the NCRB 2023 data, which shows that despite a chargesheet rate of over 70 per cent, only 20-36 per cent of cases result in convictions for major crimes;
(b) the number of Fast Track Special Courts (FTSCs) and exclusive POCSO Courts operational as of March 2025 and the case disposal and conviction rates since 2020;
(c) the State-wise average trial time taken in FTSCs and POCSO Courts; and
(d) whether the Ministry proposes to link FTSCs data to the National Judicial Data Grid (NJDG) for transparency and monitoring?

(a) whether the Department of Justice continues to rely on the Ministry of Home Affairs for its personnel requirements despite fifteen years of separation;
(b) if so, the steps taken to establish an independent cadre unit for the Department and the timeline proposed therefor; and
(c) the sanctioned strength, working strength and vacancy details of each post in the Department as of March 2025?

(a) year-wise unemployment rate among male and female graduates and post graduates in the formal sector since 2020;
(b) the parameters or criteria adopted by Government to classify individuals as employed or unemployed and whether these have been revised since 2020;
(c) the number of operational National Career Service Centres (NCSCs) currently functioning, State-wise;
(d) the number of Scheduled Caste (SC) and Scheduled Tribe (ST) candidates that have been given guidance/coaching/training through NCSCs, year-wise and category-wise; and
(e) the rate of their employment, year-wise and State-wise?

(a) total number of Eklavya Model Residential Schools (EMRS) approved, currently operational and number of students enrolled, State-wise/UT-wise;
(b) status of proposed centralization of EMRS administration under National Education Society for Tribal Students (NESTS);
(c) details of enrolment and drop-out rates of students, especially those belonging to the Particularly Vulnerable Tribal Groups (PVTGs), State-wise/UT-wise;
(d) how many EMRS currently meet the infrastructural, staffing and curricular benchmarks envisaged (comparable to Navodaya Vidyalaya Samiti schools); and
(e) the reasons for the delay in making regional offices functional, in recruitment for vacancies and in standardisation of processes across States?

(a) total number and value of National Highway projects sanctioned during the last five years which are currently delayed, along with the current status of the project;
(b) total number and value of highway projects which have been bid out but construction is yet to begin, including the reasons for no commencement;
(c) the steps being taken by Government to expedite these delayed projects to avoid cost-escalation; and
(d) how does Government plan to bring all delayed or uninitiated highway projects back on schedule?

(a) the State-wise percentage and absolute number of Public Distribution System Ration Cards that have completed e-KYC verification as on 31st October 2025;
(b) the State-wise percentage and number of Ration Card holding individual beneficiaries who have completed e-KYC verification;
(c) whether there is a backlog of pending applications for new Ration Cards or for addition of family members under National Food Security Act and State schemes; and
(d) if so, the number of pending applications, State-wise?

(a) the details of the total outstanding debt and payables of DISCOMs as of 30th October, 2025;
(b) the details of the Ujwal DISCOM Assurance Yojana (UDAY) goals, along with the status of viability, DISCOM-wise;
(c) the number of States’ DISCOMs that met UDAY targets for loss reduction; and
